    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passed. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for E.164 telephones in `OwnerRestControllerV1.normalizeTelephone`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`): after the existing general 8\u201315 digit E.164 check, I added a country-code-specific national-length rule:\n- `+61` (Australia) requires exactly **9** national digits\n- `+1` (NANP) requires exactly **10** national digits\n\nA wrong length throws `InvalidTelephoneException`, which the existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice` maps to **HTTP 400**. I also updated the method's Javadoc to document the new rule.\n\nThe new test `errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` (posts `+61 123`, expecting 400) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0). Existing valid payloads remain accepted \u2014 the seed/`uniqueTelephone` numbers normalize to `+61` with exactly 9 national digits.",
